  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "game-description-46452ebe-1d67-4f22-b12c-b69a0cdae7b1-0",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "Guitar Hero translates rock performance into a rhythm game played with a guitar-shaped controller. Players hold fret buttons and strum as notes reach a target line, maintaining timing through increasingly demanding patterns. The controller does not reproduce ordinary guitar technique, but it gives performance a physical, theatrical quality beyond pressing buttons on a standard pad."
    },
    {
      "id": "game-description-46452ebe-1d67-4f22-b12c-b69a0cdae7b1-1",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "html": "The first game appeared on PlayStation 2 in 2005. Its mixture of familiar songs, difficulty levels, and performance feedback made practice and mastery legible to players while also making the game entertaining to watch."
    },
